A||||1||fiero87||V-6 Swap?||||5||
Z||000000||fiero87||08-11-2000||12:05 PM||||Hi,<P>I am in the process of restoring an 87 fiero sport coupe.  I have never been satisfied with hp of the stock 2.5, and have been thinking about other options.  I'm not an expert mechanic, but most of my friends have no problem taking things apart, swapping engines, etc.  What i need to know here is what are my options for simple engine swaps?  If there is such a thing....I have been considering a 2.8 from a stock GT or SE.. But what other 2.8's can i use?  How about ones from Berreta's, Camaro's, etc??  Will these bolt in place of the fiero 2.8?  Any other idea's you can provide would be helpfull.  Thanks<BR><P>------------------<BR>Tim<BR>87 Fiero SC <BR>90 Daytona VNT(1 of 596)<BR>94 Duster (Winter ride)||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||08-11-2000||03:29 PM||||One thing to keep in mind, if you decide to go with a MFI or SFI V6 (e.g. the 2.8), is that you'll need to change to the higher-pressure fuel pump (meaning you'll have to remove the gas tank) to support the 40-50psi fuel-injection systems.<P>Plus, you'll have to get the computer that goes with the new engine.  Based upon what I've <B>read</B> in this forum (not <B>done</B>), 2.8's and 3.1's bolt right in.  3.4's require a few simple modifications.  Most other swaps require much more extensive work.<P>I suppose you <B>could</B> get away from changing the fuel pump and do away with the computer if you went with a carbureted engine.<P>I don't think I would want a non-fuel-injected engine, myself.  But, what do I know?  I haven't done an engine swap.  Hopefully, at this point, some of the other members will share some wisdom  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.||||reg||4
